§§ `X-claim-time: a liability claim can be time-barred before it exists`

-- GC4(g): the written claim within 30 days "from the day of the event". A third party who
-- demands compensation on day 45 after an Occurrence leaves the Insured nothing to claim on
-- in time; GC1 makes the deadline a condition precedent. Law 08/2022/QH15 art 30(3) (aid,
-- lines 715-717) runs the period from the third party's demand.
