§§ `X-award: an arbitral award the Insured wins is forfeited after 12 months`

-- GC10: the award is "final and binding". GC7(b)(ii): benefit is forfeited for claims decided
-- by arbitration without the Insured's challenge within 12 months. An award cannot be
-- appealed, so every arbitrated claim is forfeited a year after the award.
